Three fixes to daslang's LLVM JIT (modules/dasLLVM/daslib), against the
official release bundle v0.6.4-RC2 (the files are identical at commit
1524b3bf62e7decbfe530dc5f2e794b296fa1e68). Never applied to an installed
toolchain of this project; verified on a scratch copy of modules/dasLLVM
loaded with `daslang -load_module <copy> ...`. Regression tests that fail
without and pass with these hunks are in notes/upstream_cases/tests/.

1. `reinterpret<uint64>(@@fn)` emitted an invalid bitcast from the function
   aggregate `{ ptr }` to i64 and aborted codegen. The pointer is extracted
   from the aggregate and converted with ptrtoint.
2. The mirror image, `reinterpret<SomeFn>(handle)` from a 64-bit integer,
   emitted `bitcast i64 to { ptr }`; the pointer is built with inttoptr and
   inserted into an undef function aggregate.
3. A module-qualified builtin call (`math::sqrt`) reached the float-op1
   intrinsic emitter with the qualified spelling, producing the intrinsic
   name "llvm.math::sqrt.f32"; LLVMLookupIntrinsicID answers 0 and
   LLVMGetIntrinsicDeclaration dereferences it (SIGSEGV during codegen for
   sqrt floor ceil round sin cos log exp2 log2 floori ceili sinh cosh tanh).
   The namespace is stripped and id 0 is refused with a diagnostic.

